Restore the v0.7.4 lifecycle dispatch, so the tag gate's smoke run MUST go red.

This is a MUTATION FIXTURE, never a change anyone should land. It reverts the one line
`cd3fd3dec33e429fddb0a2acfe5a1d4bc2f01428` fixed, putting the reader back on the shared
`uv run --script` route that `runtime_admission()` in scripts/ccodex_sdlc.py refuses by name
("expected direct -I -B execution"). That regression shipped in BOTH published prereleases,
v0.7.3 and v0.7.4, because no gate executed the archive; issue #9 is the record.

.github/workflows/release.yml's `mutation` job applies this file to a scratch checkout, rebuilds
the archive from the mutated tree, and requires `mise run release:smoke --expect-refusal` to
report the failure by name. A gate that stays green with this applied has stopped proving
anything, so the job fails when the smoke PASSES.

The mechanism is a patch file rather than `git revert cd3fd3d` on purpose: a revert makes an
ancient commit load-bearing CI history, which a later squash or re-root would turn into a hard
error, and it would also revert that commit's tests. A patch that no longer applies also fails
the job -- the right direction -- and names bin/ccodex as the file to re-derive it from.

RE-ANCHORED 2026-08-25 (agentic-sdlc-7a2b W3a). The route it regresses did not change, but its
CASE ARM did: `ccodex sdlc <verb>` is retired, and the six lifecycle verbs are top-level, so
`run_sdlc_python` is now reached from TWO arms -- the `install|update|uninstall|doctor|recover`
table and the `status` arm's selector branch. BOTH are mutated here, because a patch that left
either intact would let a smoke case take the fixed route and report green on a regressed tree.

Re-derive after an intended change to that route:
  1. edit EVERY `run_sdlc_python "$@"` call site in bin/ccodex to `run_python ccodex_sdlc.py "$@"`
  2. git diff -U6 -- bin/ccodex   (keep this preamble; `git apply` ignores it)
  3. git checkout -- bin/ccodex

diff --git a/bin/ccodex b/bin/ccodex
index 957d0f7..399b13a 100755
--- a/bin/ccodex
+++ b/bin/ccodex
@@ -311,23 +311,23 @@ case "$route" in
   # ---- the lifecycle verb table (ratified decision 1, agentic-sdlc-7a2b) --------------------
   # Every verb decision -- admit, refuse by name, or hand off to a per-verb module -- belongs to
   # scripts/ccodex_sdlc.py, so the argument vector INCLUDING the verb is forwarded unchanged and
   # nothing is shifted here. `status` is the one collision with this command's existing surface and
   # is resolved below rather than silently reassigned.
   install|update|uninstall|doctor|recover)
-    run_sdlc_python "$@"
+    run_python ccodex_sdlc.py "$@"
     ;;
   status)
     # The ONLY name shared by the gateway plane and the lifecycle. Both survive, and neither is
     # guessed at: the lifecycle read is selected by the presence of a selector flag the gateway route
     # has never taken, and every other `ccodex status` is the gateway supervision verb it has always
     # been. A selector-shaped argv whose selectors are incomplete reaches the reader and is refused
     # there by name, so `ccodex status --agent claude` never silently forwards `--agent claude` to
     # the gateway.
     if has_lifecycle_selector "$@"; then
-      run_sdlc_python "$@"
+      run_python ccodex_sdlc.py "$@"
     fi
     shift
     dispatch_launcher_verb status "$@"
     ;;
   ensure|launch|ultracode|restart|configure)
     shift
